# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_extractor_dart.py" "DART GATE: PASS" "Dart extractor: .dart files yield class/def nodes via tree-sitter-language-pack" "Dart extractor: .dart files (Flutter/Dart) now produce class-kind and def-kind structural nodes. Root cause: .dart was in SOURCE_EXT (so file nodes were minted) but absent from GRAMMAR_BY_EXT and ts_languages -- the grammar was never loaded and the extractor produced 0 structural edges for every Dart file. No standalone tree-sitter-dart wheel exists on PyPI; grammar is loaded from tree-sitter-language-pack 0.9.x (ABI v14, compatible with tree-sitter 0.23.x). Node spec: class_definition/enum_declaration/extension_declaration mint class nodes (all have a name field); function_signature mints def nodes (covers both top-level functions and class methods). mixin_declaration omitted (no name field in this grammar version). sym_use: superclass (extends clause) emits a calls-class edge to the base type name via the existing precision guards. Call/import edges deferred to v2 (Dart call AST is identifier+selector chains with no call_expression node; import AST has no named child fields -- both require a bespoke extractor similar to Elixir). BEFORE: 417 .dart files in flutter/samples -> 0 def/class nodes. AFTER: 417 .dart files -> 2279 def/class nodes. Never-crash: malformed or empty .dart files return a bare file node. Absent language-pack: .dart files fall back to file-node direct-collision path (recall-safe, never fatal). Content-free: no literal source body in graph." "Dart extractor: class + enum + extension mint class nodes; top-level and method function_signature mint def nodes; extends clause emits sym_use calls edge to base type; all nodes carry content-free line spans; malformed .dart never crashes; canary literal not in graph" 12
